      "sound_toggle_hint": "Silences the engine rumble, radio chatter, suit breathing and every alert tone.",
      "task_0": "Pick a difficulty, look over the mission profile, then press Begin Mission.",
      "task_1": "Watch the Saturn V climb. When the banner turns green you are in orbit — press Proceed to Orbit.",
      "task_10": "Read your flight record — four graded calls — then fly again and beat it.",
      "task_2": "Timing call: wait for the green burn window, then fire TLI. Firing early is allowed, but it costs a correction later.",
      "task_3": "Answer the knowledge check, decide on the mid-course correction if one is offered, then head for lunar orbit.",
      "task_4": "Watch one orbit: loss of signal behind the Moon, Earthrise, then undock for the descent.",
      "task_5": "Fly the landing: W or ↑ for thrust, A/D to slide. Touch down under 3 m/s down and 5 m/s sideways.",
      "task_6": "Walk the surface: collect 4 rocks with F, deploy the seismometer, then End EVA.",
      "task_7": "Watch the ascent and docking, then fire the TEI burn to head home.",
      "task_8": "Answer the second knowledge check, set the entry angle inside the corridor, then begin re-entry.",
      "task_9": "Watch the entry and splashdown, then complete the mission.",
      "unmute_mission_audio": "Turn mission sound back on",
      "your_job_now": "Your job now: ",
      "a11y_animated_re_entry_and_recovery_capsule_motion_heating_and_parachutes_follow_the_entry_mode": "Animated re-entry and recovery. Capsule motion, heating and parachutes follow the entry model. Before parachute deployment, the spherical Earth horizon uses measured altitude and a 60 degree vertical field. The geometric horizon dip is available in the instruments. A shallow entry can skip out. After splashdown, illustrative recovery begins just before sunrise: uprighting bags roll the capsule upright, then swimmers fit a flotation collar. Read the instruments and use playback controls below to inspect any moment.",
