      "stress_analysis_deep_beam_approximatio": "Stress analysis (deep-beam approximation)",
      "stress_test": "Stress Test",
      "students_can_build_a_simple_section_mo": "Students can build a simple section-model wind tunnel from a box fan, a length of cardboard for an airfoil-like deck cross-section, and rubber bands as springs. Hang the cross-section on rubber bands in the airflow + slowly increase the fan speed. Bluff-shaped sections (rectangular cardboard) flutter at relatively low wind speeds; streamlined sections (curved + tapered) remain stable at higher speeds. This is exactly the same principle that distinguished the original Tacoma deck from modern long-span bridge cross-sections. The Khan Academy + Bridge Design + Engineering YouTube channels have demonstrations.",
      "submersible_submerged_floating_bridges": "Submersible (submerged-floating) bridges",
      "subsea_bored_tunnel": "Subsea bored tunnel",
      "success_cases": "Success cases",
      "sundial_bridge": "Sundial Bridge",
      "supports_pin_left_roller_right": "Supports: pin (left) ▲  ·  roller (right) ▲⊙",
      "surface_materials": "Surface materials",
      "suspension_bridge_cable_shape": "Suspension bridge cable shape",
      "suspension_bridges_work_differently_fr": "Suspension bridges work differently from trusses. The deck hangs from cables; cables hang in a curve between towers; towers transfer the load down. The cables are in PURE TENSION, the towers in PURE COMPRESSION. Anchorages resist the horizontal pull of the cables — they're typically massive concrete blocks buried in bedrock at each end of the bridge.",
      "suspension_desc": "The deck hangs from cables, which hang in a curve between two tall towers. The cables are in tension; the towers are in compression. Anchorages at each end resist the cable tension.",
      "sustainable_design_strategies": "Sustainable design strategies: ",
      "sustained_high_wind_sites": "Sustained high-wind sites",
      "swing_bridge": "Swing bridge",
      "synchronization_beginning": "Synchronization beginning: ",
      "tacoma_narrows_flutter_animation": "Tacoma Narrows flutter animation",
      "tactical_floating_causeway_inls": "Tactical Floating Causeway / INLS",
      "target_safety_factor": "Target safety factor",
      "target_safety_factor_2": "Target safety factor",
      "technical_design": "Technical design",
      "technique_how_it_works": "Technique + how it works",
      "temperature_sensors": "Temperature sensors",
      "tendons_are_tensioned_before_concrete_": "Tendons are tensioned BEFORE concrete is poured + before it cures. Once concrete hardens + bonds to the tendons, anchors are released; the tendons pull inward through friction. Used for FACTORY-MADE beams (highway girders, double-tees, hollow-core planks).",
      "tension": "Tension",
      "test_facilities_around_the_world": "Test facilities around the world",
      "test_with_the_people_who_depend_on_it": "Test with the people who depend on it: ",
      "the_1981_walkway_collapse_was_a_connec": "1981 年空中走道倒塌事故是一起接頭失效。後期設計變更將原本懸吊兩層走道的一根長吊桿改成兩根較短吊桿（下層改吊於上層之下），使上層接頭載重瞬間加倍，卻無人重新檢算。事故造成 114 人罹難、216 人受傷。簽證負責工程師須負最終責任——兩位主責工程師皆遭撤銷密蘇里州技師執照。此案現已成為工程倫理課程的經典教材。",
      "the_akashi_kaiky_bridge_was_being_buil": "The Akashi-Kaikyō Bridge was being built when the M6.9 Hyogoken-Nanbu (Kobe) earthquake hit on January 17, 1995. The two towers moved 1 METER farther apart. Engineers redesigned the deck mid-construction to accommodate the new geometry. The bridge survived + opened in 1998. A real-world case study in seismic resilience under extreme + unpredictable conditions.",
      "the_big_idea": "The big idea",
      "the_challenge": "The challenge",
      "the_conceptual_foundations_come_from_r": "有限元素的概念根基源自 Richard Courant 的變分法（1943 年）與更早的手算結構分析法（傾角變位法，1915 年）。現代 FEA 於 1950–60 年代主要為飛機結構分析而發展（波音三角翼結構）。關鍵推手包括柏克萊的 Ray Clough（1960 年創造「有限元素法」一詞）、倫敦帝國學院與斯圖加特的 John Argyris，以及斯旺西的 Olek Zienkiewicz（1967 年撰寫奠基教科書，至今仍廣受引用）。1970 年代大型電腦普及後，橋梁工程界導入 FEA；到了 2000 年，全球幾乎每座大型橋梁皆使用 FEA 軟體（ANSYS、ABAQUS、SAP2000、MIDAS、LUSAS）設計。",
      "the_deck_has_entered_an_aeroelastic_fl": "The deck has entered an aeroelastic flutter mode. Each oscillation creates lift forces that amplify the next oscillation — a positive feedback loop. Unrestrained, it grows until structural failure. The historical Tacoma Narrows collapsed at ~42 mph in 1940.",
      "the_framing_that_matters": "The framing that matters: ",
      "the_honest_critique": "The honest critique: ",
      "the_hyatt_regency_lesson": "The Hyatt Regency lesson: ",
      "the_institutional_reality": "The institutional reality: ",
      "the_iron_bridge": "The Iron Bridge",
      "the_members_are_usually_not_what_fails": "最常先失效的往往不是桿件本身，而是桿件之間的接頭。Hyatt Regency（1981 年）、Silver Bridge（1967 年）、Tay Bridge（1879 年）皆始於接頭——吊桿接頭、眼桿孔耳、斜撐接板。現代橋梁工程對接頭的重視程度絲毫不亞於主構件。",
      "the_mesh_matters": "The mesh matters",
      "the_minneapolis_bridge_collapsed_durin": "明尼亞波利斯大橋於傍晚尖峰時段倒塌，奪走 13 條人命並致 145 人受傷。調查指出肇因於設計瑕疵（節點板厚度不足）疊加施工載重（橋面堆置鋪面材料）。2008 年完工的替代橋（St. Anthony Falls 大橋）在施工階段即裝設數百個感測器——應變計、加速度計、溫度感測器與腐蝕感測器，成為全球監測最密集的橋梁之一。這場悲劇大幅提升美國橋梁界對結構健康監測（SHM）技術的關注。",
      "the_morandi_bridge_genoa_italy_collaps": "The Morandi Bridge (Genoa, Italy) collapsed in August 2018, killing 43. Built 1967 as a prestressed cable-stayed design with concrete-encased stays. Decades of corrosion ate the steel wires inside the concrete encasement — invisible from outside. The encasement (the very feature meant to protect the steel) prevented inspection from detecting the deterioration. Modern designs use replaceable stays + non-encased prestressing where possible.",
      "the_roebling_lineage": "The Roebling lineage: ",
      "the_technical_tools_for_bridge_monitor": "過去 20 年來，橋梁監測的技術工具進展神速。但真正落實這些工具的制度能量——感測器裝設經費、資料分析專業人力、明確權責分工，以及出現警訊時果斷封橋修繕的政治決心——進展卻遠遠落後。1967 年以來的多起重大橋梁悲劇（Silver、Mianus、I-35W、Morandi/Genoa、Pittsburgh Fern Hollow）既是技術失誤，更是制度失靈。",
      "the_us_infrastructure_picture": "The US infrastructure picture: ",
      "thicker_larger_force": "Thicker = larger force",
      "thickness_moj": ", thickness shows magnitude. Forces are solved exactly by the method of joints — every member force satisfies equilibrium at both of its ends.",
      "thickness_shows_magnitude_forces_calcu": ", thickness shows magnitude. Forces calculated using the deep-beam approximation (real analysis would use method of joints or matrix structural analysis).",
      "three_seismic_design_strategies": "Three seismic design strategies: ",
