      "some_species_also_have_photoreceptors_": "Some species also have photoreceptors NEXT TO their photophores. They detect their own output + adjust it. This closed-loop control is what makes real counter-illumination so precise.",
      "some_species_turn_the_tables_a_50kg_gi": "Some species turn the tables. A giant Pacific octopus at the Seattle Aquarium was filmed killing dogfish sharks that shared its tank (footage made for PBS around 2000). But the next year, a larger shark might eat THAT octopus. Predator/prey labels are size-relative + life-stage-relative.",
