      "designer_bookbinders": "Designer Bookbinders",
      "designers_call_this_the_letter_s_skele": "Designers call this the letter's \"skeleton\" plus its \"skin.\" The skeleton (basic structure) survives across centuries; the skin (proportions, contrast, terminals) marks the era. A type historian can usually date an unattributed book within 50 years just by looking at the lowercase a.",
