      "arc_load_preset": "⚙ Load starting settings",
      "arc_m_cold_ask": "Which ONE change flattens the ropey bead the most?",
      "arc_m_cold_goal": "Start from a cold, ropey MIG bead on 1/4\" steel and fix it: no lack of fusion, a profile that is not ropey, and penetration near target.",
      "arc_m_cold_h1": "A steep toe angle means the metal is sitting on the plate instead of wetting into it.",
      "arc_m_cold_h2": "Flatten it with voltage, then add heat (amperage up or travel down) until lack of fusion disappears.",
      "arc_m_cold_status": "Toe angle {value1} ({value2}). Lack of fusion severity: {value3}. Penetration {value4} of the plate.",
      "arc_m_cold_title": "Fix the cold, ropey bead",
      "arc_m_cold_why": "Voltage controls how the puddle wets out. Amperage and travel speed mostly change how much metal lands, not its shape.",
      "arc_m_load_first": "⚙ Load the starting settings first: this mission is about fixing that bead. Your prediction is not locked yet.",
      "arc_m_lowheat_ask": "Doubling travel speed will make heat input:",
      "arc_m_lowheat_goal": "Reach 70% penetration on 3/8\" steel using no more than 10% above the least heat input that can do it.",
      "arc_m_lowheat_h1": "Extra heat past the target does not make the joint stronger; it grows the heat-affected zone and the distortion.",
      "arc_m_lowheat_h2": "Watch the macro-etch: get the fusion zone just past the dashed 70% line, then stop adding heat.",
      "arc_m_lowheat_status": "Penetration {value1} of the plate (need 70%). Heat input {value2}; the least that reaches 70% is {value3}, so pass at or under {value4}.",
      "arc_m_lowheat_title": "Deep enough, no hotter",
      "arc_m_lowheat_why": "Travel speed is in the denominator of the heat-input formula: double it and each inch gets half the heat.",
      "arc_m_need_hand": "This mission needs the Top-down view in Hands-on torch mode, and a full pass laid by hand.",
      "arc_m_need_preset": "This mission starts from a bad bead: press Load starting settings first, then fix it.",
      "arc_m_notyet": "❌ Not yet — adjust and check again",
