      "car2_me_pick": "Pick a starting path. You will see its first two years, then make two decisions (at 20 and at 22) and watch the pay, credentials and trade-offs add up to age 26. Pay is in 2026 Maine dollars, built from the bands quoted in this module.",
      "car2_me_reset": "↺ Clear my two choices",
      "car2_me_run": "running {value1}",
      "car2_me_side": "+ {value1} side-shop income",
      "car2_me_start_pay": "{value1} start",
      "car2_me_std": "The standard track, milestone by milestone (no detours)",
      "car2_me_sum_mine": "By age 26 your path ({value1}, then {value2}, then {value3}) earned {value4} before taxes.",
      "car2_me_sum_title": "Summary: your path against the alternatives",
      "car2_me_tab_road": "🗺 Roadmap + decisions",
      "car2_me_tn_ext": "Contact one Maine employer (BIW HR or a small shop) and ask 3 questions: How do you hire? What's the first 6 months like? What separates the welders who stay from the ones who quit? Then put the real wage they quote into the roadmap rows by hand and recompute your running total. Real conversation > brochure.",
      "car2_me_tn_m1": "\"All welding pays the same\" — varies 2-3× across processes + employers. Pipe welding > production MIG > truck body work.",
      "car2_me_tn_m2": "\"You need a 4-year degree to make good money\" — false in this field. In the roadmap model a BIW welder earns about {value1} in year 2 and {value2} in year 5 with regular overtime, plus a pension, with no degree.",
      "car2_me_tn_m3": "\"Union work is for older guys\" — locals actively recruit young apprentices. Apply at 18-22 and you journey out in your early-to-mid 20s.",
      "car2_me_tn_m4": "\"The path that pays most by 26 is the best path\" — the top total in the roadmap is usually pipeline travel: months away, unpaid gaps, no shop of your own. A total is one input, not the answer.",
      "car2_me_tn_q1": "Why does BIW have an internal training program rather than only hiring trained welders?",
      "car2_me_tn_q2": "What's the trade-off between union apprenticeship and going straight to a small shop after CTE?",
      "car2_me_tn_q3": "Use the roadmap: from your chosen start, which pair of decisions earns the most by 26, and what does it trade away? Would you choose it anyway?",
      "car2_me_tn_q4": "Choose \"Take CWI prep\" from two different starts. Why does the EMCC graduate sit the CWI exam a year earlier than the BIW trainee?",
