      "cons7_low": "Too little",
      "cons7_low_aria": "Low-flow schematic: a short, partial shielding envelope leaves gaps above the molten pool. Dashed pink arrows point from the surrounding atmosphere toward the pool.",
      "cons7_low_caption": "Insufficient gas flow can leave the pool without enough shielding. The gaps and inward arrows show how surrounding atmosphere can reach it; the concern in this lesson is porosity.",
      "cons7_modes": "Shielding gas flow regime",
      "cons7_note": "Qualitative schematic, not a flow simulation. The regimes do not set a CFH value or predict coverage, defect counts or weld quality for a real setup. Dots and arrows identify atmosphere and gas paths; they are not amounts or particle counts.",
      "cons7_recommended": "Equipment-recommended range",
      "cons7_recommended_aria": "Recommended-range schematic: shielding gas extends from the nozzle to cover the molten pool. Surrounding atmosphere is shown outside the envelope; this does not establish a flow setting.",
      "cons7_recommended_caption": "Use the machine’s recommended range, adjusted for breeze and nozzle distance. The continuous envelope focuses attention on gas coverage around the pool.",
      "cons8_ceriated_gray_r2": "gray",
      "cons8_choose": "Tungsten classification to inspect",
      "cons8_class_caption": "The box identifies the electrode classification. Compare the printed designation even when two reference paint colors look alike.",
      "cons8_class_label": "Printed classification",
      "cons8_color_label": "Reference paint color",
      "cons8_compare": "Compare two classifications",
      "cons8_focus_class": "2 · Printed classification",
      "cons8_focus_group": "Electrode detail to inspect",
      "cons8_focus_paint": "1 · Painted identification end",
      "cons8_focus_prep": "3 · Lengthwise grinding marks",
      "cons8_identification_heading_r2": "Tungsten electrodes — painted identification end",
      "cons8_intro": "Select a reference electrode, then inspect its identification end, package designation or grinding direction. Color names and classifications stay readable below the drawing.",
      "cons8_model_note": "Schematic references on the same scale. The rod, box and grinding marks stay fixed; only the selected identification information and outline change. No electrode size, tip angle, machine setting or weld-quality prediction is shown.",
      "cons8_paint_caption": "The painted end is an identification cue. Read its color name together with the printed classification and product instructions.",
      "cons8_peer_label": "Comparison classification",
      "cons8_prep_caption": "The four lines run lengthwise, parallel to the rod. They locate the grinding direction; their spacing and the flat-ended rod do not specify a prepared tip shape.",
      "cons8_product_identification_r2": "Tungsten color codes depend on the applicable standard edition and product. Current manufacturer charts list EWCe-2/WC20 as gray (formerly orange); EWG blends can use maker-specific colors. Read the printed classification and the electrode manufacturer’s instructions instead of identifying an electrode by paint alone.",
      "cons8_reference": "Read all nine reference entries",
      "cons8_reference_box": "REFERENCE BOX",
      "cons8_reference_intro_r2": "Select a reference electrode to inspect its printed classification and identification color. Color names accompany every reference.",
      "cons8_scene_aria": "Reference electrode and package: {value1}. Paint color: {value2}. Highlighted: {value3}.",
      "cons8_source_ck": "CK Worldwide · current electrode identification",
      "cons8_source_inverter": "Miller · AC inverter electrode preparation",
      "cons8_source_miller": "Miller · tungsten identification and preparation",
      "cons8_teacher_preparation_r2": "How do electrode type and power source affect tungsten preparation, and why should you check the electrode and machine manufacturer’s instructions?",
      "cons8_title": "Inspect the paint, read the box",
      "cons8_tungsten_preparation_r2": "Tungsten preparation depends on the electrode and power source. Grinding marks should run lengthwise along the electrode. Modern inverter AC TIG can use a pointed or truncated electrode instead of a pre-balled tip. Follow the electrode and machine manufacturer’s preparation instructions, including how to handle contaminated tungsten.",
      "cons8_use_label": "Use in this reference",
