      "home_saved_pass": "Saved pass · {value1} of {value2} segments",
      "hull_plating_hsla_65_hsla_80_hy_80_hy__r2": "Hull plating (HSLA-65, HSLA-80, HY-80, HY-100 high-strength steels). Internal structure (bulkheads, frames). Piping systems (carbon steel + stainless + copper-nickel). Aluminum superstructure (sometimes). Every weld is inspected. Navy work follows NAVSEA rules rather than AWS D1.1: Technical Publication 248 (welder + procedure qualification), Tech Pub 278 (piping, machinery, pressure vessels) and MIL-STD-1689 (surface-ship hull structure).",
      "hunt6_crop_aria": "Locked close-up of committed finding {value1}, {value2}, at a light angle of {value3} degrees.",
      "hunt6_current_light": "Current light · {value1}°",
      "hunt6_distinguish": "What distinguishes it",
      "hunt6_empty": "Classify a feature to add its evidence here. Each committed first call gets a numbered place on the review map.",
      "hunt6_findings": "Committed findings to review",
      "hunt6_first_call": "Your committed first call",
      "hunt6_help": "Review the evidence behind your committed first calls. Choose a numbered finding; its close-up stays locked while you continue inspecting elsewhere.",
      "hunt6_identified": "Feature identified",
      "hunt6_lighting": "Compare lighting",
      "hunt6_map_aria": "Map of {value1} committed findings. Selected finding {value2}, {value3}. Only committed observations have numbered labels.",
      "hunt6_next": "Next finding →",
      "hunt6_note": "The map contains committed observations, including normal features and mistaken calls. Lighting uses the same specimen renderer. Section replay is available only when that finding was committed from an actual cut; reviewing spends no cuts and changes no first-call scores.",
      "hunt6_observation": "Recorded evidence",
      "hunt6_open": "Review committed evidence →",
      "hunt6_overhead": "Overhead light · 90°",
      "hunt6_prev": "← Previous finding",
