      "pwht_heating_the_welded_part_to_a_targ_r2": "PWHT = heating the welded part to a target temperature, holding for a specified time, then cooling. Different PWHT types serve different purposes:",
      "pwht_is_expensive_large_parts_need_wal_r2": "PWHT is EXPENSIVE: large parts need walk-in furnaces or wrapped electric heaters, and slow heat-up, hold and cool cycles can take days of energy and labor. Shops price it into code-work bids, and designers sometimes keep sections under the code's thickness limit specifically so PWHT is not required.",
