      "sym2_m_ann_reset": "Practice reset: new numbers, score and streak cleared.",
      "sym2_m_answer": "Your answer",
      "sym2_m_answer_is": "Answer: {value1}.",
      "sym2_m_bad": "✗ Not quite: you entered {value1}. Rework it, or open the worked solution.",
      "sym2_m_bp_go": "Open the mini blueprint →",
      "sym2_m_bp_link": "Try it on a real layout: the Symbols Reader has a three-view bracket drawing with four symbols to read.",
      "sym2_m_build_go": "Open the Symbol Builder →",
      "sym2_m_build_link": "Reading is half of it. In the Symbol Builder you write the symbol from a work order and get every field checked.",
      "sym2_m_consts": "Constants used: 1 in = 25.4 mm exactly; carbon steel 0.2836 lb/in³; representative deposition efficiency 95% for solid GMAW wire, 85% for FCAW, 60% for SMAW (stub loss, slag and spatter). Check your consumable maker's data for real jobs.",
      "sym2_m_first_bad": "first try missed",
      "sym2_m_first_ok": "★ first try",
      "sym2_m_h_bid1": "Labor = hours × hourly shop rate (dollars per hour × hours = dollars).",
      "sym2_m_h_bid2": "Total = labor + materials + overhead.",
      "sym2_m_h_brace1": "The rise is OPPOSITE the angle and the brace is the hypotenuse. SOH: sine = opposite ÷ hypotenuse.",
      "sym2_m_h_brace2": "Rearrange: brace = rise ÷ sin(angle).",
      "sym2_m_h_filler1": "Cross-section area = leg × leg ÷ 2 (square inches). Times the weld length in inches gives the volume.",
      "sym2_m_h_filler2": "Weld metal = volume × 0.2836. Filler to buy = weld metal ÷ deposition efficiency (as a decimal), because stubs, slag and spatter never end up in the joint.",
      "sym2_m_h_frac2dec1": "Divide the top number by the bottom number.",
      "sym2_m_h_frac2dec2": "Each 1/{value1} in is {value2} in. Multiply by the top number, then add any whole inches.",
      "sym2_m_h_frac2mm1": "First turn the fraction into a decimal inch.",
      "sym2_m_h_frac2mm2": "Then multiply the decimal inches by 25.4.",
      "sym2_m_h_mm2frac1": "Divide millimetres by 25.4 to get decimal inches.",
      "sym2_m_h_mm2frac2": "Multiply the decimal inches by 16, round to a whole number, and put it over 16.",
      "sym2_m_h_plate1": "Volume = length × width × thickness, in cubic inches. Use the thickness as a decimal.",
      "sym2_m_h_plate2": "Weight = volume × 0.2836 lb per cubic inch.",
      "sym2_m_h_square1": "The diagonal is the hypotenuse of a right triangle: a² + b² = c².",
      "sym2_m_h_square2": "Square each side, add them, then take the square root.",
      "sym2_m_h_square2t": "These sides are a multiple of 3-4-5. Find the multiplier and use it on the 5.",
      "sym2_m_h_tape1": "Find the last whole-inch number to the left of the marker.",
      "sym2_m_h_tape2": "Count the ticks past that inch. Each small tick is 1/16 in; the 1/2 tick is the longest, then 1/4, then 1/8.",
      "sym2_m_hint_btn": "Hint {value1} of {value2}",
      "sym2_m_intro": "New numbers every round. Your first check on each set of numbers is the one that scores. Hints are free; the worked solution opens after you try.",
      "sym2_m_invalid": "Type a number, a fraction like 7/16, or a mixed number like 1-3/8.",
      "sym2_m_mm_rule": "Metric: 1 in = 25.4 mm exactly. 1/16 in ≈ 1.6 mm, 1/8 in ≈ 3.2 mm, 1/4 in ≈ 6.4 mm, 1/2 in ≈ 12.7 mm.",
      "sym2_m_new": "New numbers",
      "sym2_m_ok": "✓ Correct: {value1}.",
      "sym2_m_overview_practice": "Every topic ends with checked practice: type an answer, get it checked, ask for hints, then see the worked solution. The Checked practice tab above has all nine problem types in one place.",
      "sym2_m_p_bid": "Bid a repair job: {value1} h of shop time at ${value2} per hour, ${value3} of steel and parts, and ${value4} overhead for gas, consumables and cylinder rental. What is the total bid in dollars?",
      "sym2_m_p_brace": "A brace climbs {value1} in at {value2}° from horizontal. How long is the brace along its length? (To the nearest 1/16 in, or 2 decimal places.)",
      "sym2_m_p_filler": "You will weld {value1} ft of {value2} in equal-leg fillet with {value3}. How many pounds of filler metal should you buy? Assume a flat-faced fillet (area = leg × leg ÷ 2), weld metal at 0.2836 lb/in³, and a deposition efficiency of {value4}%.",
      "sym2_m_p_frac2dec": "Convert {value1} in to a decimal inch (3 decimal places).",
      "sym2_m_p_frac2mm": "Convert {value1} in to millimetres (1 decimal place). One inch is exactly 25.4 mm.",
      "sym2_m_p_mm2frac": "A metric plate is {value1} mm thick. What is that to the nearest 1/16 in? (Type a fraction like 3/8 or a decimal.)",
      "sym2_m_p_plate": "A steel plate is {value1} in × {value2} in × {value3} in thick. How much does it weigh, in pounds? Carbon steel weighs 0.2836 lb per cubic inch (about 490 lb/ft³).",
      "sym2_m_p_square": "A rectangular frame is {value1} in by {value2} in. If its corners are square, what should the diagonal measure? (To the nearest 1/16 in, or 2 decimal places.)",
      "sym2_m_p_tape": "Read the tape at the orange marker. Type the reading in inches: a mixed number like 3-7/16 or a decimal.",
      "sym2_m_proc_fcaw": "FCAW flux-cored wire",
      "sym2_m_proc_gmaw": "GMAW solid wire",
      "sym2_m_proc_smaw": "SMAW stick electrodes",
      "sym2_m_reset": "↺ New numbers + reset score",
      "sym2_m_s_bid": "Labor = {value1} h × ${value2}/h = {value3}. Total = {value3} + ${value4} + ${value5} = {value6}.",
      "sym2_m_s_brace": "Brace = {value1} ÷ sin({value2}°) = {value1} ÷ {value3} = {value4} in. The horizontal run is {value1} ÷ tan({value2}°) = {value5} in.",
      "sym2_m_s_filler": "Area = {value1} × {value1} ÷ 2 = {value2} in². Length = {value3} ft × 12 = {value4} in. Weld metal = {value2} × {value4} × 0.2836 = {value5} lb. Filler = {value5} ÷ {value6} = {value7} lb.",
      "sym2_m_s_frac2dec": "{value1} ÷ {value2} = {value3}. Add {value4} whole inches: {value5} in, or {value6} in to 3 places.",
      "sym2_m_s_frac2mm": "{value1} in = {value2} in. {value2} × 25.4 = {value3} mm, or {value4} mm to 1 place.",
      "sym2_m_s_mm2frac": "{value1} ÷ 25.4 = {value2} in. {value2} × 16 = {value3}, which rounds to {value4} sixteenths = {value5} in.",
      "sym2_m_s_plate": "Volume = {value1} × {value2} × {value3} = {value4} in³. Weight = {value4} × 0.2836 = {value5} lb.",
      "sym2_m_s_square": "√({value1}² + {value2}²) = √{value3} = {value4} in. Measure both diagonals: if they match this, the frame is square.",
      "sym2_m_s_tape": "{value1} whole inches + {value2}/16 in = {value3} in ({value4} in as a decimal).",
