      "tech2_rob_next_point": "Next point",
      "tech2_rob_next_try": "Now turn on \"Load the next part 5 mm off\" and run the same program. Real parts never sit exactly where the first one did.",
      "tech2_rob_off": "OFF",
      "tech2_rob_on": "ON",
      "tech2_rob_pass": "✓ Weld complete: seam fully covered, no faults.",
      "tech2_rob_right": "Cursor right",
      "tech2_rob_run": "▶ Run program",
      "tech2_rob_shift_explain": "The part arrived 5 mm off and the robot did exactly what it was taught: it welded where the seam USED to be. This is why cells use seam finding. Turn on seam tracking and run the same program again.",
      "tech2_rob_shift_off": "Load the next part 5 mm off (off)",
      "tech2_rob_shift_on": "⚠ Next part arrived 5 mm off (on)",
      "tech2_rob_sort_aria": "Job {value1}: robot or manual",
      "tech2_rob_sort_intro": "Would a shop put each job on a robot (or cobot), or give it to a manual welder? Think volume, repeatability, fit-up and where the work is. Your first pick counts.",
      "tech2_rob_sort_manual": "🧑‍🏭 Manual welder",
