      "dx_copperband_butterflyfish_behavior": "Encountered singly or in pairs; adults form pairs during breeding.",
      "dx_copperband_butterflyfish_diet": "Small animals living on the bottom, reached by probing cracks and holes in the reef.",
      "dx_copperband_butterflyfish_habitat": "Shallow coastal reefs, rocky shores, bays and estuaries in the Indo-West Pacific, often in sheltered or silty water.",
      "dx_copperband_butterflyfish_observe": "Locate the real eye in its orange bar, then look toward the tail to find the false eyespot. Compare its long snout and broad bars with a threadfin butterflyfish.",
      "dx_coral_tree_nursery_behavior": "Hanging fragments are kept off the bottom while they grow to a size suitable for planting.",
      "dx_coral_tree_nursery_diet": "The frame does not feed. Its suspended living corals use sunlight and capture food.",
      "dx_coral_tree_nursery_habitat": "In-water coral nurseries, where fragments can be grown above the seabed before outplanting.",
      "dx_coral_tree_nursery_observe": "Identify the central pole, crossbars and hanging lines, then distinguish nursery fragments from reef-attached colonies.",
      "dx_crown_of_thorns_behavior": "Feeding leaves a pale patch of bare skeleton; unusually large outbreaks can remove extensive living coral.",
      "dx_crown_of_thorns_diet": "Consumes living coral tissue, frequently feeding on branching and plate-forming Acropora.",
      "dx_crown_of_thorns_habitat": "Coral-rich reef areas, often sheltered within branches or beneath plates during the day.",
      "dx_crown_of_thorns_observe": "Look for many thorn-covered arms and a nearby feeding scar while keeping clear of the spines.",
      "dx_day_octopus_behavior": "Forages in daylight and can quickly alter its skin color and texture.",
      "dx_day_octopus_diet": "Hunts crabs, clams and snails, probing small spaces with its arms.",
      "dx_day_octopus_habitat": "Reef rock and rubble with holes that can be used as dens.",
      "dx_day_octopus_observe": "Search for an eye, an arm outline or a texture change beside a den before looking for the whole body.",
      "dx_deeper": "A little deeper",
