      "dx_firefish_behavior": "Often seen alone or as a pair, hovering above a nearby refuge rather than joining a large school.",
      "dx_firefish_diet": "Zooplankton carried by the current, including copepods and crustacean larvae.",
      "dx_firefish_habitat": "Sandy patches and burrows on the upper parts of outer reef slopes in the Indo-Pacific.",
      "dx_firefish_observe": "Compare the tall pennant with its slim body, then check the rounded tail and pale-to-red color change.",
      "dx_foliose_coral_behavior": "A shared stony skeleton grows outward in thin sheets with paler growing margins.",
      "dx_foliose_coral_diet": "Algal partners supply energy, and the animal polyps also capture tiny drifting food.",
      "dx_foliose_coral_habitat": "Protected upper reef slopes, where thin plates can form overlapping tiers or curling whorls.",
      "dx_foliose_coral_observe": "Look along a plate for radial ridges and rows of tiny cups between them.",
      "dx_free_learning": "Every profile is open to explore. Choose a species to study it, save favorites, or compare look-alikes.",
      "dx_giant_clam_behavior": "The exposed mantle carries rows of tiny eyes and can withdraw into the protective shell.",
      "dx_giant_clam_diet": "Symbiotic algae supply energy; the clam also filters particles from the water.",
      "dx_giant_clam_habitat": "Shallow reefs and lagoons, often with part of the heavy shell embedded in reef material.",
      "dx_giant_clam_observe": "Find the colorful living mantle between the shell halves and look for the paired water openings.",
      "dx_giant_moray_behavior": "The repeated opening of its mouth moves water over its gills for breathing.",
      "dx_giant_moray_diet": "Feeds mostly on fishes, with some crustaceans also taken.",
      "dx_giant_moray_habitat": "Reef holes and crevices that conceal its long body while the head remains visible.",
      "dx_giant_moray_observe": "Look for a black gill patch and spotted head from outside the crevice, without reaching in.",
      "dx_giant_triton_behavior": "Uses scent to locate prey and hunts across the reef, often at night.",
      "dx_giant_triton_diet": "Sea stars, including crown-of-thorns, and other echinoderms such as sea cucumbers.",
      "dx_giant_triton_habitat": "Hard and sandy bottoms around coral reefs across the tropical Indo-Pacific.",
      "dx_giant_triton_observe": "Follow the spiral ridges toward the pointed tip, then turn the specimen to study the orange opening, striped edge and small lip teeth.",
      "dx_green_turtle_behavior": "Breathes air and alternates underwater activity with visits to the surface.",
      "dx_green_turtle_diet": "Adults mainly graze seagrasses and algae; diet can vary with life stage and location.",
      "dx_green_turtle_habitat": "Coastal feeding grounds, including shallow seagrass and algal habitats near reefs.",
      "dx_green_turtle_observe": "Check its blunt beak and smooth shell while leaving a clear path to the surface.",
      "dx_habitat": "Where it lives",
      "dx_harlequin_shrimp_behavior": "Often found in pairs near a reef shelter. The petal-like antennules move as the shrimp samples chemical cues from the water.",
      "dx_harlequin_shrimp_diet": "Specializes in sea stars, including Linckia species. It eats tube feet and other soft tissue using specialised feeding limbs.",
      "dx_harlequin_shrimp_habitat": "Sheltered holes and crevices in tropical coral reefs across the Indian and Pacific oceans, including Hawai‘i and documented eastern Pacific reefs.",
      "dx_harlequin_shrimp_observe": "Compare the broad paddles and large blotches with the cleaner shrimp’s long white antennae and striped back. Trace the separate head structures, jointed limbs and curved abdomen rather than relying on colour alone.",
      "dx_hawksbill_turtle_behavior": "Its narrow pointed beak helps it reach food in small reef openings.",
      "dx_hawksbill_turtle_diet": "Specializes in sponges while also eating other invertebrates and some algae.",
      "dx_hawksbill_turtle_habitat": "Coral reefs and other coastal feeding grounds with sponge-rich crevices and resting ledges.",
      "dx_hawksbill_turtle_observe": "Compare the hawk-like beak and overlapping shell plates with the green turtle's rounded features.",
      "dx_humphead_wrasse_behavior": "A slow-moving, long-lived fish whose prominent forehead develops as it grows.",
      "dx_humphead_wrasse_diet": "Eats hard-bodied invertebrates and fishes, including some animals avoided by many other predators.",
      "dx_humphead_wrasse_habitat": "Indo-Pacific reefs, with large individuals moving among coral formations and reef slopes.",
      "dx_humphead_wrasse_observe": "Compare the thick lips and rounded head with the sharper beak and steep face of a bumphead parrotfish.",
      "dx_identified_badge": "Identified on a dive",
