      "fig_ac_aria": "Scale of aragonite saturation from 0 to 5. In tropical waters it was about 4.2 before industry and about 3.5 by 2010. Above 1, corals can still build. Below, building speed: each 1 unit drop makes corals build roughly 15% slower, about 85% of the speed before, and studies vary widely.",
